    not_duplicate_of: []  # 2626
    pr_ref:  # 2626
    description: "SECURITY.md states, of the audited IO surface: \"Hypergumbo's safety claims are verified by\nhypergumbo verify-claims docs/hypergumbo.claims.yaml against an analysis of its own source code.\nThe per-entry-point analysis below states what each CLI subcommand is allowed to do; regressions\nland as taint-flow findings and FAIL THE GATE.\"\n\nThere is no gate. Verified on dev c675fc484f: grep -rn 'verify-claims' .github/workflows/ returns\nZERO hits across all five workflow files. The only in-suite reference is\ntest_verify_claims.py::test_shipped_self_claims_file_loads_clean, which asserts that the claims\nfile PARSES (len(claims) > 0, all entries carry ids). It never computes a verdict. So no regression\ncan fail anything, and none ever has.\n\nThis is a DOCUMENTATION defect, not an analysis finding: it holds regardless of what the taint\nmachinery does next, which is why it is filed separately from the parked self-audit adjudication\n(see the discussion entry below).\n\nRELATED UNGATED OBLIGATION: ADR-0016 section 4 Phase 4 obliges \"a GitHub Action / CI step that runs\nclaim verification on every PR\", and the ADR-0017 counterpart obliges the self-audit invocation.\nBoth are unhonoured. ADR-0016 carries an unqualified 'Status: Accepted', so per docs/adr/README.md\n(\"a grep of the status line must not lie\") that status is overclaiming on this point.\n\nTWO RESOLUTIONS, and they are NOT equivalent:\n  (a) Correct the sentence - say what is actually true (claims are verified on demand; there is no\n      CI gate). One-line docs fix. Leaves ADR-0016 section 4 Phase 4 unhonoured but stops the\n      false assertion.\n  (b) Build the gate - makes the sentence true, but gating merges on the current finding set is\n      exactly what the parked-adjudication decision declined, because the finding set is produced\n      by an instrument under active repair and a baseline seeded now would be INVERTED (fixing\n      WI-votom's unearned-False routes UN-suppresses real leaks and RAISES the unsanitized count,\n      so a shrink-only ceiling would fail on the correctness fix and read a suppression regression\n      as progress).\nThis item is scoped to (a). (b) is deliberately out of scope until the instrument is calibrated.\n\nIf (a) is taken, ADR-0016 section 4 Phase 4 should be amended in place at the same time so the\ncontract and the docs stop disagreeing - otherwise this item closes and the ADR still asserts a\ngate nobody built.\n\nMEASURED CONTEXT, for whoever picks this up: the self-run on 2026-08-05 was exit 1, 18 verdicts,\n16 confirmed, 2 violated (runtime-cli-no-host-fs 1,148 unsanitized / 1,428 sanitized;\nruntime-cli-no-subprocess 742 unsanitized / 0 sanitized), 0 inconclusive. Do NOT cite those counts\nas a baseline - see the parked-adjudication rationale."  # 2626
    fields: {}  # 2626
- op: discuss  # 4616
  at: '2026-08-05T21:25:23Z'  # 4616
  by: agent  # 4616
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4616
  clock: 2  # 4616
  nonce: '4616'  # 4616
  message: "PARKED (owner decision, 2026-08-05): the self-audit ADJUDICATION is deferred; only the two instrument-independent facts were filed.\n\nWHAT IS PARKED: adjudicating the 1,890 unsanitized flows on the two violated claims (runtime-cli-no-host-fs 1,148; runtime-cli-no-subprocess 742), and resolution (b) on this item -- building the verify-claims CI gate that ADR-0016 section 4 Phase 4 obliges.\n\nOWNER RATIONALE: the mechanism that GENERATES these findings is itself in flux. Adjudicating an unstable instrument spends effort on a set whose membership is scheduled to change. Specifically, on dev c675fc484f:\n  - the sanitized label is earned by _ddg_taint_reaches returning False, and WI-votom-tuvik-bikof-kazuh-vonuv-mimag-jajoj-torig records TWO VERIFIED routes to an unearned False, so the 1,428 / 1,148 split on runtime-cli-no-host-fs is a direct function of a predicate known to be wrong in a known direction;\n  - inclusion is still decided by call-graph BFS, not data flow (INV-sadah-gifob-nujob-tovan-kinos-vovuk-kupon-mibuj clause S2; dataflow_scope.py emits inclusion_decided_by = call_graph_reachability). 990 of the 1,148 carry ddg_mixed, but the DDG chose only the LABEL;\n  - the walk cannot remove anything: 16 confirmed / 40 unknown / 0 REFUTED over 56 walks (INV-busis-povul-butun-kosut-tozik-jarok-vokaz-vomur, 2026-08-05), so the finding set is an over-approximation BY CONSTRUCTION and the pending work is what shrinks it;\n  - both evidence rows sampled carry confidence = approximate. The tool says so itself.\n\nTHE INVERTED-BASELINE ARGUMENT (this is why parking is not merely thrift): a baseline seeded from todays counts would point the wrong way. verify_claims.py computes a verdict from taint_label, sink_zone and sanitized, with matching = flows that are NOT sanitized. Fixing WI-votom UN-SUPPRESSES real leaks and therefore RAISES the unsanitized count. A shrink-only ceiling on that quantity would FAIL on the correctness fix and read a suppression regression as PROGRESS. Adjudicating now does not just waste effort -- it manufactures a wrong reference point that then has to be argued back down.\n\nWHAT IS NOT PARKED, and why: two facts survive the argument because neither rests on the taint walk.\n  1. WI-fasuv-lisov-nakul-gavid-guhuj-pohas-bomif-zurul -- the runtime git subprocess, established by READING repo_fingerprint.py:109 and its call path, not by trusting the analysis. True whatever the machinery does next.\n  2. This item -- SECURITY.md asserts a gate that does not exist. A documentation defect, independent of any finding.\n\nRE-EVALUATION TRIGGER (so this parking does not expire silently the way the INV-zogud deferral did): revisit the adjudication when the walk’s False is EARNED -- concretely, when WI-votom is done AND INV-lupav-bigak-zirob-gofun-sopod-sirij-panal-dinav clauses L2 and L3 are closed -- or when INV-busis receives its ADR-0017 section 7a/7b ruling, whichever comes first. Until one of those happens, do NOT cite the 18/16/2 verdict split or the 1,890-flow figure as a baseline for anything."  # 4616
