- op: discuss  # 2392
  at: '2026-08-09T23:40:10Z'  # 2392
  by: agent  # 2392
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2392
  clock: 4  # 2392
  nonce: '2392'  # 2392
  message: "RESOLVED. The gate exists, it BLOCKS, and SECURITY.md's text is now true. Closed on\nBEHAVIOURAL evidence per the closure-evidence rule, not on a proxy -- this item's\nstatement is about runtime behaviour (a CI gate that fails), so \"the file exists\" would\nnot have been sufficient.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES: .github/workflows/full-suite.yml, step \"Self-claim drift gate\n(WI-vanun)\", running `PYTHON=python ./scripts/check-self-claims`. It sits in full-suite\nrather than per-PR because it runs a full self-analysis, and PYTHON is passed explicitly\nbecause the bare `hypergumbo` console script is exit 127 in CI (the meta-package is\nnever installed there) -- an earlier draft keyed on `command -v hypergumbo` and would\nhave SKIPPED WITH EXIT 0 in the only place it matters.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, both directions, run today:\n\n  CLEAN ARM   ./scripts/check-self-claims\n              -> exit 0, \"OK -- 18 claims unchanged (16 inconclusive, 2 violated)\"\n\n  DRIFT ARM   perturbed ONE verdict in docs/hypergumbo.claims.expected.json\n              (add-extras-no-dev-zone: inconclusive -> confirmed), re-ran:\n              -> exit 1, \"check-self-claims: SELF-CLAIM DRIFT\n                          changed: add-extras-no-dev-zone: confirmed -> inconclusive\"\n              and the message requires updating BOTH the snapshot and SECURITY.md,\n              stating that updating the snapshot alone \"recreates the drift this gate\n              exists to catch\". Snapshot restored afterwards; `git status` clean.\n\nSo the gate is not merely present -- it is reachable, it fails closed, and it refuses\nthe exact one-sided fix that would hollow it out.\n\nADR-0016 section 4 Phase 4 item 1 (\"CI step that runs claim verification on every PR\")\nis satisfied by BUILDING the gate. The amendment this item once contemplated -- softening\nthe ADR or the doc to match reality -- is NOT needed and should not be made; reality was\nmoved to match the doc instead, which was the right direction.\n\nWHAT CHANGED UNDERNEATH THIS ITEM, worth recording because it inverts the numbers filed\nabove. This item's MEASURED CONTEXT block records the 2026-08-05 self-run as \"18\nverdicts, 16 CONFIRMED, 2 violated, 0 inconclusive\". Today the same command reports 18\nverdicts, 16 INCONCLUSIVE, 2 violated, 0 confirmed. That is not a regression: PR #251\nfixed verify-claims certifying claims it had never actually checked, so hypergumbo now\nconfirms ZERO of its own claims and says so. The item's own instruction not to cite the\n18/16/2 split as a baseline was correct and is now correct for a second reason.\n\nTHE PARKED ADJUDICATION STAYS PARKED, and its trigger is only HALF fired. The recorded\ncondition was: revisit when WI-votom is done AND INV-lupav clauses L2 and L3 are closed,\nor when INV-busis receives its section 7a/7b ruling. WI-votom is done. INV-lupav L2\ncloses through WI-joluk, which is still todo_hard and unstarted, so L2/L3 are NOT closed.\nINV-busis has received no ruling -- and section 7b has now been re-priced DOWN three\ntimes without ever being asked, because the arm that would consume the result does not\nrun. So the trigger has NOT fired. Do not adjudicate the 1,890 flows yet, and do not\ncite that figure as a baseline."  # 2392
- op: discuss  # 78e5
  at: '2026-08-10T07:44:24Z'  # 78e5
  by: agent  # 78e5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 78e5
  clock: 5  # 78e5
  nonce: '78e5'  # 78e5
  message: "S10 COHERENCE SWEEP, 2026-08-10. Two spec paragraphs were asserting the opposite of the\ncode, both in the taint section, both found by cross-reading a measurement against the\ndocument rather than by reading the document alone.\n\n1. VERDICT TABLE said \"Inconclusive (no DDG) | *Specified, never emitted.*\" while\n   `inconclusive` is the MAJORITY outcome: hypergumbo's own pinned expected verdicts are\n   16 inconclusive / 2 violated / 0 confirmed (docs/hypergumbo.claims.expected.json).\n   Both statements were true of DIFFERENT producers -- verify_taint_claim still does not\n   emit the ADR-0017 section 3c sense, while the capability gate (_taint_blind_reason,\n   INV-javam / WI-kajil) emits it constantly and is what refuses to certify a claim the\n   analysis could not check. The table now names both producers, quotes the 16/2/0\n   split, and carries the known residual (a language emitting ONE token call edge still\n   looks covered -- pinned as test_language_with_a_token_call_edge_still_falsely_confirms).\n\n2. FUNCTION SUMMARIES said \"*Implemented, no production consumer* ... no taint code path\n   calls infer_summary or load_function_summaries today.\" Half false, and the load-\n   bearing half: taint.py:2557 calls load_function_summaries in propagate_taint_ddg, and\n   taint.py:2085 already carried the correction in a docstring -- it was never propagated\n   to the spec. Section 4a (infer_summary) genuinely has zero callers; section 4b runs.\n   The distinction is not pedantic: S8 measured 8 of 26 call-node escape sites (30.8%) as\n   \"summary key present, no summary entry\", i.e. a CATALOGUE gap in a live mechanism.\n\n3. FIELD-SENSITIVITY LITE was RE-VERIFIED rather than inherited (is_field_tainted still\n   has zero callers outside its definition) and now carries the re-verification date,\n   because its sibling claim above went stale by exactly the route of being copied\n   forward unchecked.\n\nADR-0016 SECTION 4 PHASE 4: NO AMENDMENT MADE, DELIBERATELY. The plan lists it as S10\nwork, but WI-vanun's thread already ruled it out: the obligation (\"CI step that runs\nclaim verification on every PR\") was satisfied by BUILDING the gate, so reality was moved\nto match the doc rather than the reverse. Softening the ADR would now make it wrong."  # 78e5
